                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "unbreakable"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " option is taller than a single page, it will not be advanced and, instead, break across pages. In this case, the automatic orphan protection is still applied."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The converter does not honor the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "unbreakable"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " option on all content blocks in AsciiDoc, such as lists and paragraphs. In these cases, the author can elect to wrap the content in an open block with the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "unbreakable"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " option."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "[%unbreakable]\n--\nIf this paragraph does not fit in the remaining space on this page,\nand it is short enough to fit on a page by itself,\nthe converter will advance it to the next page so it does not break.\n--"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Internally, the open block enclosure is exactly how "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "unbreakable"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is supported on tables."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "The logic in the converter that calculates the extent of a block, which includes its title, main content, and padding, uses multiple passes, called “dry runs”, to get an accurate measurement of where a block begins, ends, and whether it breaks across pages. When the converter determines that a block’s title and anchor would be orphaned, or that a block breaks when it’s marked as unbreakable, it has to advance to the next page and convert it again in order to redo the extent calculation. This logic is vital for decorating the block with a border and background because the extent must be pixel accurate. All these dry runs add additional processing time and effort to the conversion."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Making all blocks unbreakable by default adds a lot of extra steps (not to mention leaving behind a lot of gaps in the document). Orphan prevents adds almost as many since it’s a similar process. Doing that by default for tables, sections, and discrete headings would be too complex and costly. To recoup some of the processing time, we decided to make some trade-offs. Therefore, blocks are breakable by default and authors must opt-in to get orphan prevention for tables, sections, and discrete headings."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "However, you can add the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "breakable"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " (or "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "unbreakable"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " option) to any block at runtime using an Asciidoctor extension. Refer to "
                  },
                  {
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "breakable tables"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "xref",
                    "target": "extend:use-cases.html#breakable-tables"
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " to find the code for this extension."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
